A||||9||mrfixit58||Getting Ready for Daytona - Need Advice||||6||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||03-12-2001||04:34 PM||||Well, This is the last week I'll be driving the GT. It goes into the garage this weekend and the clean-up begins. I'm planning on entering the car in the street stock / daily driver class. <P>I'm going to start by removing the seats for some repair work and by replacing the old worn-out carpet for some old not-quite-so worn-out carpet. Then, if there's time, I may paint the black trim strip (advise?).<P>My questions are about the general clean-up. What do you folks recommend when it comes to the exterior prioity clean-up? Front trunk first? Engine bay first? followed by wash and wax? How much disassembly should I do? What is most important, what is a waste of time?<P>What types of cleaners do you recommend? What type of vinyl protection (Armor All?)? The list can go on and on. Please feel free to interject if I've not covered it here.<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||87GT||03-12-2001||07:08 PM||||Im kind of in the same boat here.  I dont really need to mess with the interior since its pretty much perfect, but I do want to find some kind of touch up black paint for the sides on either side of the rear deck lid.  I am also putting on my new dew wipes this coming weekend, and my new hinge pins and bushings for the driver door.  So much work and so little time. I am in the SCMC class.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||03-12-2001||09:10 PM||||If the engine compartment is greasy, I'd start there.  Blowing that dirt all over a cleaned car, means you clean it again.  I'm driving to Daytona 1300 miles or so.  I start cleaning Thursday when I blow into town.  The car had been cleaned before it was put away in October.  It looked pretty good when I dug it out of the snow last Friday.  I go to the carwash near the hotel, and clean the 1300 miles of crud off the car.  Last year it rained all the way down.  At least I didn't have a lot of road tar.  The car gets washed at least twice (I love the diamond spoke wheels).  Some Mequires, cleaners, polishes and waxes.  The car cleans up quite well.  Lots of cotton towles for wiping and polishing.  If it wasn't below freezing now, I'd been cleaning now.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||03-12-2001||09:24 PM||||If you are going to paint up your trim, go right now to your dealer and get a bunch of the mounting clips. You WILL break most of them taking the trim off. <P>Lar <BR>I'm leaving Sun. but I'm going to my mothers place firs to get the 1300 miles of grime off before I show up at the Holiday Inn on Thurs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||09:51 PM||||Mrfxit; Depends on what you want you may be too late. You can be judge with either the front or rear trunk open or both. That means that if your engine compartment and front trunk is dirty you leave that close to avoid points taken out. So I would start cleaning/fixing the exterior and then the interior before anything else. Then if you have time you can go to the front or rear trunk.<BR>When doing the exterior make sure you do the inner gas door area. You need to have that open & usualy is very dirty.<BR>You can paint the trims on the car or off. If you are careful you can take them out without braking anything. I did it once. Go to an auto paint store and get a good trim paint. You can use that for the grills and any black part in the car. Just remember that when you detail an area and it start to look good then the area next to it will look worse. And it goes on and on and on. I started my car in January. The front trunk took me two weeks (wkend + week nights). But it looks brand new now and I added a carpet in that area. I have until next weekend to finish the engine & paint some interior parts. I don't want to do anything the week of the show. I'm so tired already!! Good luck.. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||03-12-2001||10:40 PM||||Here's a tip I heard of... <BR>Before you hit the road, spray the front of the car with PAM. Will stop all the bugs from sticking to your fascia. Just wash it off when you get there.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||03-12-2001||11:48 PM||||Phil and Larry, you two have a great time down there!! Sorry I won't make that show (a little too far from San Francisco!!) but I may show up at the National show with my gold GT or maybe even my blue GT........we'll just have to see........||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfixit58||03-13-2001||07:22 AM||||A lot of good advise so far. What about the types of cleaning products and protective coatings. What are your favorites and why?<P><BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000008||RossT||03-13-2001||07:31 AM||||I use Zaino products from <A HREF="http://www.zainobros.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zainobros.com</A> <P>GOOD STUFF!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||03-13-2001||07:59 AM||||I use Mequiars but heard only good things about Zaino. Will have to try it.||||reg||1
